tt-local-generator (0.60.3) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(gif): stop a heavy animated GIF from freezing the whole app. Both GIF
    drivers (drive_gif_animation + AnimatedGifWidget._tick) decoded each frame
    on the GTK main thread and re-armed at the frame delay regardless of decode
    cost, so a large AnimateDiff GIF whose per-frame decode exceeded its delay
    starved the main loop (UI lockup, confirmed via py-spy: MainThread parked in
    artgen_render._tick / libpixbufloader-gif). Both ticks now self-throttle:
    never re-arm sooner than the frame decode itself took, so the main loop
    always gets breathing room — the GIF animates slower, never frozen.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 11:58:29 -0700

